<div id="A5.SS2.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">To construct <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{1},\mathbf{y}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{1},\mathbf{y}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Phi}_{1},\bm{\Phi}_{2,1}\in\mathcal{MLP}(m_{1}r_{1},m_{1},\lceil\log_{2}N_{\mathrm{mlp}}\rceil^{2},\lceil N_{\mathrm{mlp}}/4\rceil,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>mlp</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>mlp</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Phi}_{1},\bm{\Phi}_{2,1}\in\mathcal{MLP}(m_{1}r_{1},m_{1},\lceil\log_{2}N_{\mathrm{mlp}}\rceil^{2},\lceil N_{\mathrm{mlp}}/4\rceil,B)</annotation></semantics></math> using Lemma <a href="#Thmconj219" title="Lemma 19 (Theorem 1 of []). ‣ E.2 Construction of multilayer perceptron layers ‣ Appendix E Construction of the Transformer ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> such that
for any <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{4}\in[-1,1]^{(r_{1}-1)m_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{4}\in[-1,1]^{(r_{1}-1)m_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, any <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{1}\in[-1,1]^{m_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{1}\in[-1,1]^{m_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and any <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{3}\in[-1,1]^{m_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{3}\in[-1,1]^{m_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
