<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Directional Convergence of the Nadaraya–Watson Estimator</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we prove Lemma <a href="#Thmconj26" title="Lemma 6. ‣ 5 Proof Sketch of the Upper Bound for the Approximation Error ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.
Unless specified otherwise, the implicit constants in the notation <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lesssim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≲</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lesssim</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{O}</annotation></semantics></math> depend only on <math id="A6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{1},m_{2},r_{1},r_{2},\delta_{1},\delta_{2},\beta_{2},\sup_{\mathbf{h}\in\mathcal{H}}\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathcal{C}^{\beta_{2}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{1},m_{2},r_{1},r_{2},\delta_{1},\delta_{2},\beta_{2},\sup_{\mathbf{h}\in\mathcal{H}}\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathcal{C}^{\beta_{2}}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmconj26" title="Lemma 6. ‣ 5 Proof Sketch of the Upper Bound for the Approximation Error ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{W}\coloneqq\{\mathbf{e}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{e}_{W}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{W}\coloneqq\{\mathbf{e}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{e}_{W}\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of tokens. The following lemma characterizes the Markovian dynamics of the token generation process.
Its proof is deferred to Appendix <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix F Directional Convergence of the Nadaraya–Watson Estimator ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmconj228" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmconj228.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 28</span></span><span id="Thmconj228.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmconj228.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmconj228.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj228.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="Thmconj228.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmconj228.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}=(\mathbf{Z}_{n})_{n\in\mathbb{N}_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}=(\mathbf{Z}_{n})_{n\in\mathbb{N}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a homogeneous <math id="Thmconj228.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>-valued Markov chain with transition probability kernel</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx145" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex351"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex351.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{z})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex351.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{Z}_{n+1}=\mathbf{z}|\mathbf{Z}_{n}=\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq\mathbb{P}(\mathbf{Z}_{n+1}=\mathbf{z}|\mathbf{Z}_{n}=\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex352"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex352.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\,=c(\mathbf{x})\exp(g(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{z}))\prod_{i=1}^{r-1}\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{x}_{i+1}),\quad\mathbf{x}=(\mathbf{x}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{x}_{r})\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r},\quad\mathbf{z}=(\mathbf{z}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{z}_{r})\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.448em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\,=c(\mathbf{x})\exp(g(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{z}))\prod_{i=1}^{r-1}\mathbb{I}(\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{x}_{i+1}),\quad\mathbf{x}=(\mathbf{x}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{x}_{r})\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r},\quad\mathbf{z}=(\mathbf{z}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{z}_{r})\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmconj228.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj228.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmconj228.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\colon\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}\times\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\colon\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}\times\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a bounded function and <math id="Thmconj228.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalizing constant. Then <math id="Thmconj228.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a unique stationary distribution <math id="Thmconj228.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx146" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex353"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex353.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(e^{2\|g\|_{\infty}}W)^{-r}\leq\rho(\mathbf{z})\leq(e^{-2\|g\|_{\infty}}W)^{-r},\quad\text{for all}\ \mathbf{z}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(e^{2\|g\|_{\infty}}W)^{-r}\leq\rho(\mathbf{z})\leq(e^{-2\|g\|_{\infty}}W)^{-r},\quad\text{for all}\ \mathbf{z}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmconj228.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj228.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Furthermore, for any <math id="Thmconj228.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1,2,\ldots," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1,2,\ldots,</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx147" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex354"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex354.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}}\|P^{n}(\mathbf{x},\cdot)-\rho\|_{\operatorname{TV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}}\|P^{n}(\mathbf{x},\cdot)-\rho\|_{\operatorname{TV}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex354.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Big(1-e^{-2\|g\|_{\infty}r}\Big)^{n/r}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Big(1-e^{-2\|g\|_{\infty}r}\Big)^{n/r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The next lemma shows that, for a uniformly exponentially ergodic Markov chain on a countable state space, if the direction of the conditional expectation of a vector-valued function satisfies a smoothness condition, then the direction of the Nadaraya–Watson estimator based on a truncated trajectory converges to that of the corresponding conditional expectation.
For a unit vector <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the projection matrices <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\bm{\theta}}\coloneq\bm{\theta}\bm{\theta}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\bm{\theta}}\coloneq\bm{\theta}\bm{\theta}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\perp}_{\bm{\theta}}\coloneq I_{d}-\bm{\theta}\bm{\theta}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\perp}_{\bm{\theta}}\coloneq I_{d}-\bm{\theta}\bm{\theta}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> projects onto the direction of <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\perp}_{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\perp}_{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> projects onto the subspace orthogonal to <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
See (<a href="#A1.E29" title="In Appendix A Additional Notation ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) for the definition of <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\sum}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>∑</mo><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\sum}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmconj229" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmconj229.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 29</span></span><span id="Thmconj229.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmconj229.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmconj229.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj229.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}\coloneq(\bm{\xi}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝛏</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}\coloneq(\bm{\xi}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a homogeneous Markov chain on a countable set <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D},</annotation></semantics></math> which admits a unique stationary distribution <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho.</annotation></semantics></math> Assume that <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly exponentially ergodic, i.e. there exists a constant <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathbf{M}}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝐌</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathbf{M}}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0,1,\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0,1,\ldots</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex355" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex355.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\|P^{n}(\mathbf{x},\cdot)-\rho\|_{\operatorname{TV}}\leq c_{\mathbf{M}}^{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\|P^{n}(\mathbf{x},\cdot)-\rho\|_{\operatorname{TV}}\leq c_{\mathbf{M}}^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmconj229.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj229.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-step transition probability of <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We write <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}^{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}^{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the probability and expectation of the Markov chain <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> started at <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\xi}_{0}=\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝛏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\xi}_{0}=\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a bounded function <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}\colon\mathcal{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}\colon\mathcal{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> define</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex356" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex356.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\mathbb{E}^{\mathbf{x}}[\mathbf{f}(\bm{\xi}_{1})],\qquad\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})\coloneq\frac{\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})}{\big\|\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\big\|_{2}},\quad\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\mathbb{E}^{\mathbf{x}}[\mathbf{f}(\bm{\xi}_{1})],\qquad\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})\coloneq\frac{\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})}{\big\|\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\big\|_{2}},\quad\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmconj229.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj229.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where we assume that <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\|\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\|\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math> In addition, assume that for some bounded function <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}:\mathcal{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}:\mathcal{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\bm{\theta}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝛉</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\bm{\theta}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
it holds</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx148" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})-\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})\|_{2}\leq c_{\bm{\theta}}\|\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})-\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})\|_{2}^{\beta},\quad\quad\text{for all}\ \mathbf{x},\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{D}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})-\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})\|_{2}\leq c_{\bm{\theta}}\|\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})-\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})\|_{2}^{\beta},\quad\quad\text{for all}\ \mathbf{x},\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{D}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmconj229.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj229.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex357" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex357.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\cdot)\coloneqq\overline{\sum}_{t\in[\log^{2}T,T-\log^{2}T]}\Big(K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}_{t}),\mathbf{s}(\cdot)\big)\,;\,\mathbf{f}(\bm{\xi}_{t+1})\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\cdot)\coloneqq\overline{\sum}_{t\in[\log^{2}T,T-\log^{2}T]}\Big(K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}_{t}),\mathbf{s}(\cdot)\big)\,;\,\mathbf{f}(\bm{\xi}_{t+1})\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmconj229.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj229.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K_{\lambda}(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{\prime})\coloneq\exp(-\|\mathbf{z}-\mathbf{z}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}/(2\lambda^{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\lambda}(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{z}^{\prime})\coloneq\exp(-\|\mathbf{z}-\mathbf{z}^{\prime}\|_{2}^{2}/(2\lambda^{2}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for any <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx149" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}^{\mathbf{x}}\left[\big\|P^{\perp}_{\bm{\theta}(\bm{\xi}_{T})}\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\bm{\xi}_{T})\big\|^{2}_{2}\right]=\tilde{O}\Big(\lambda^{2\beta}+\frac{1}{T\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)]}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}^{\mathbf{x}}\left[\big\|P^{\perp}_{\bm{\theta}(\bm{\xi}_{T})}\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\bm{\xi}_{T})\big\|^{2}_{2}\right]=\tilde{O}\Big(\lambda^{2\beta}+\frac{1}{T\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)]}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmconj229.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj229.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx150" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex358"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex358.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}^{\mathbf{x}}\bigg(\big\|P_{\bm{\theta}(\bm{\xi}_{T})}\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\bm{\xi}_{T})\big\|_{2}&lt;\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\frac{\big\|\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)P_{\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})}\mathbf{m}(\bm{\xi})\right]\big\|_{2}}{4\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\big[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)\big]}\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}^{\mathbf{x}}\bigg(\big\|P_{\bm{\theta}(\bm{\xi}_{T})}\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\bm{\xi}_{T})\big\|_{2}&lt;\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\frac{\big\|\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)P_{\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})}\mathbf{m}(\bm{\xi})\right]\big\|_{2}}{4\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\big[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)\big]}\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{1}{T\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)]}+\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\big[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)\big]}{T\big\|\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)P_{\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})}\mathbf{m}(\bm{\xi})\right]\big\|_{2}^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{1}{T\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)]}+\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\big[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)\big]}{T\big\|\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)P_{\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})}\mathbf{m}(\bm{\xi})\right]\big\|_{2}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmconj229.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj229.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the implicit constants depend only on <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathbf{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝐌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathbf{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝛉</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{f}\|_{\infty}\coloneqq\max_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{f}\|_{\infty}\coloneqq\max_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\|\mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmconj229.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{s}\|_{\infty}\coloneqq\max_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\|\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{s}\|_{\infty}\coloneqq\max_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{D}}\|\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is deferred to Appendix <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix F Directional Convergence of the Nadaraya–Watson Estimator ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>.
The first assertion controls the component of <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\bm{\xi}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\bm{\xi}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> that is orthogonal to <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}(\bm{\xi}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}(\bm{\xi}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, while the second assertion ensures that the component along <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}(\bm{\xi}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}(\bm{\xi}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large with high probability.
The estimator <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> in the lemma excludes indices <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> near the boundaries <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;\log^{2}T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;\log^{2}T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;T-\log^{2}T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;T-\log^{2}T</annotation></semantics></math>.
This ensures that the estimator only uses samples which are similarly distributed as the invariant distribution and are approximately independent of <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\xi}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\xi}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmconj26" title="Lemma 6. ‣ 5 Proof Sketch of the Upper Bound for the Approximation Error ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex359" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex359.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\coloneqq(r_{1}+1)\lor r_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\coloneqq(r_{1}+1)\lor r_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, let</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx151" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex360"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex360.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\xi}_{t}\coloneqq(\mathbf{X}_{t+1},\ldots,\mathbf{X}_{t+r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\xi}_{t}\coloneqq(\mathbf{X}_{t+1},\ldots,\mathbf{X}_{t+r})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">and, for <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}=(\mathbf{x}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{x}_{r})\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=(\mathbf{x}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{x}_{r})\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx152" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex361"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex361.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{f}\big(\mathbf{x}\big)\coloneqq\frac{\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{x}_{r})}{\exp\Big(\mathbf{g}_{0}\big(\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{x}_{r-r_{1}}),\ldots,\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{x}_{r-1})\big)^{\top}\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{x}_{r})\Big)},\qquad\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\operatorname{stack}\big(\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{x}_{r-r_{2}+1}),\ldots,\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{x}_{r})\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>stack</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{f}\big(\mathbf{x}\big)\coloneqq\frac{\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{x}_{r})}{\exp\Big(\mathbf{g}_{0}\big(\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{x}_{r-r_{1}}),\ldots,\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{x}_{r-1})\big)^{\top}\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{x}_{r})\Big)},\qquad\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\operatorname{stack}\big(\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{x}_{r-r_{2}+1}),\ldots,\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{x}_{r})\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmconj228" title="Lemma 28. ‣ F.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix F Directional Convergence of the Nadaraya–Watson Estimator ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>, for given <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{h}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A6.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{\xi}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{\xi}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>
is a homogeneous Markov chain on <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which admits a unique
stationary distribution <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfying</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx153" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big(\frac{\exp(-2m_{1}\delta_{1}-2\delta_{2})}{W}\Big)^{r}\leq\rho(\mathbf{x})\leq\Big(\frac{\exp(2m_{1}\delta_{1}+2\delta_{2})}{W}\Big)^{r},\qquad\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>W</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>W</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big(\frac{\exp(-2m_{1}\delta_{1}-2\delta_{2})}{W}\Big)^{r}\leq\rho(\mathbf{x})\leq\Big(\frac{\exp(2m_{1}\delta_{1}+2\delta_{2})}{W}\Big)^{r},\qquad\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx154" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex362"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex362.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}}\|P^{n}(\mathbf{x},\cdot)-\rho\|_{\operatorname{TV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}}\|P^{n}(\mathbf{x},\cdot)-\rho\|_{\operatorname{TV}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex362.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Big(1-e^{-2r(m_{1}\delta_{1}+\delta_{2})}\Big)^{n/r},\quad n\in\mathbb{N}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Big(1-e^{-2r(m_{1}\delta_{1}+\delta_{2})}\Big)^{n/r},\quad n\in\mathbb{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-step transition probability of the Markov chain.
This implies that <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{\xi}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{\xi}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly exponentially ergodic.
We further define</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex363" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex363.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\bm{\xi}_{1})|\mathbf{h},\bm{\xi}_{0}=\mathbf{x}],\qquad\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})\coloneq\frac{\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})}{\big\|\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\big\|_{2}},\qquad\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{f}(\bm{\xi}_{1})|\mathbf{h},\bm{\xi}_{0}=\mathbf{x}],\qquad\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})\coloneq\frac{\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})}{\big\|\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\big\|_{2}},\qquad\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">Then we have the following results, whose proof is deferred to Appendix <a href="#A6.SS4" title="F.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix F Directional Convergence of the Nadaraya–Watson Estimator ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.4</span></a>.
See (<a href="#A1.E29" title="In Appendix A Additional Notation ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) for the definition of <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\sum}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>∑</mo><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\sum}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmconj230" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmconj230.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 30</span></span><span id="Thmconj230.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmconj230.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmconj230.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmconj230.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the assumptions of Lemma <a href="#Thmconj26" title="Lemma 6. ‣ 5 Proof Sketch of the Upper Bound for the Approximation Error ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and the above notation,</span></p>
<ol id="A6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A6.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,
the directions of </span><math id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex364" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex364.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\sum}_{w\in[W]}\Big(\exp\big(\mathbf{h}(\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x}))^{\top}\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{e}_{w})\big)\,;\,\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{e}_{w})\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\sum}_{w\in[W]}\Big(\exp\big(\mathbf{h}(\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x}))^{\top}\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{e}_{w})\big)\,;\,\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{e}_{w})\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.ix1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">coincide,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">there exists </span><math id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> depending only on </span><math id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{1},m_{2},\delta_{1},\delta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{1},m_{2},\delta_{1},\delta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for any </span><math id="A6.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r},</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A6.Ex365" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex365.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}\geq c_{1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{m}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}\geq c_{1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">there exists </span><math id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\bm{\theta}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\bm{\theta}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> depending only on </span><math id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{2},\delta_{2},\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathcal{C}^{\beta_{2}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{2},\delta_{2},\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathcal{C}^{\beta_{2}}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for any </span><math id="A6.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x},\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x},\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A6.Ex366" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex366.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})-\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})\|_{2}\leq c_{\bm{\theta}}\|\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})-\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})\|_{\infty}^{\beta_{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})-\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})\|_{2}\leq c_{\bm{\theta}}\|\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})-\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})\|_{\infty}^{\beta_{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iv)</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">there exists </span><math id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> depending only on </span><math id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{1},\delta_{1},\delta_{2},r_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{1},\delta_{1},\delta_{2},r_{2})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex367" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex367.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}}\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)]\geq c_{2}\varphi_{W}(\lambda)^{r_{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}}\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)]\geq c_{2}\varphi_{W}(\lambda)^{r_{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.ix5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(v)</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.ix5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with </span><math id="A6.I1.ix5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.ix5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as defined in (ii),</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex368" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex368.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}}\frac{\big\|\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)P_{\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})}\mathbf{m}(\bm{\xi})\right]\big\|_{2}}{\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\big[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)\big]}\geq\frac{c_{1}}{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝃</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\mathbf{x}\in\mathcal{E}_{W}^{r}}\frac{\big\|\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)P_{\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{x})}\mathbf{m}(\bm{\xi})\right]\big\|_{2}}{\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\big[K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{s}(\bm{\xi}),\mathbf{s}(\mathbf{x})\big)\big]}\geq\frac{c_{1}}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define random vectors <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{1,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{r_{1}m_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{1,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{r_{1}m_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A6.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{2,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{r_{2}m_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{2,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{r_{2}m_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A6.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{m_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{m_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex369" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex369.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{1,t}\coloneqq\begin{pmatrix}\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{X}_{t-r_{1}})\\
\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{X}_{t-r_{1}+1})\\
\vdots\\
\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{X}_{t-1})\end{pmatrix},\qquad\mathbf{Z}_{2,t}\coloneqq\begin{pmatrix}\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{X}_{t-r_{2}})\\
\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{X}_{t-r_{2}+1})\\
\vdots\\
\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{X}_{t-1})\end{pmatrix},\qquad\mathbf{Y}_{t}\coloneqq\frac{\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{X}_{t})}{\exp[\mathbf{g}_{0}(\mathbf{Z}_{1,t})^{\top}\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{X}_{t})]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐠</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{1,t}\coloneqq\begin{pmatrix}\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{X}_{t-r_{1}})\\
\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{X}_{t-r_{1}+1})\\
\vdots\\
\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{X}_{t-1})\end{pmatrix},\qquad\mathbf{Z}_{2,t}\coloneqq\begin{pmatrix}\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{X}_{t-r_{2}})\\
\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{X}_{t-r_{2}+1})\\
\vdots\\
\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{X}_{t-1})\end{pmatrix},\qquad\mathbf{Y}_{t}\coloneqq\frac{\bm{\phi}_{2}(\mathbf{X}_{t})}{\exp[\mathbf{g}_{0}(\mathbf{Z}_{1,t})^{\top}\bm{\phi}_{1}(\mathbf{X}_{t})]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, define</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx155" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex370"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex370.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\mathbf{Z}_{2,T+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\mathbf{Z}_{2,T+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex370.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\overline{\sum}_{s\in[\log^{2}T,T-\log^{2}T]}\Big(K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{Z}_{2,s},\mathbf{Z}_{2,T+1}\big)\,;\,\mathbf{Y}_{s}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\overline{\sum}_{s\in[\log^{2}T,T-\log^{2}T]}\Big(K_{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{Z}_{2,s},\mathbf{Z}_{2,T+1}\big)\,;\,\mathbf{Y}_{s}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex371" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex371.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\alpha}\coloneqq\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{X}_{T-r+1},\ldots,\mathbf{X}_{T})\in\mathbb{S}^{m_{2}-1},\quad P_{\bm{\alpha}}\coloneq\bm{\alpha}\bm{\alpha}^{\top},\quad P^{\perp}_{\bm{\alpha}}\coloneq I_{m_{2}}-\bm{\alpha}\bm{\alpha}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜶</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝜶</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝜶</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\alpha}\coloneqq\bm{\theta}(\mathbf{X}_{T-r+1},\ldots,\mathbf{X}_{T})\in\mathbb{S}^{m_{2}-1},\quad P_{\bm{\alpha}}\coloneq\bm{\alpha}\bm{\alpha}^{\top},\quad P^{\perp}_{\bm{\alpha}}\coloneq I_{m_{2}}-\bm{\alpha}\bm{\alpha}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Both <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\bm{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜶</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\bm{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\perp}_{\bm{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\perp}_{\bm{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> are projection matrices, where <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\bm{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜶</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\bm{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the projection onto the one-dimensional subspace <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}\bm{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜶</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}\bm{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\perp}_{\bm{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\perp}_{\bm{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the projection onto its orthogonal complement.
By (ii) and (iii) of Lemma <a href="#Thmconj230" title="Lemma 30. ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ F.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix F Directional Convergence of the Nadaraya–Watson Estimator ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>,
we can apply
Lemma <a href="#Thmconj229" title="Lemma 29. ‣ F.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix F Directional Convergence of the Nadaraya–Watson Estimator ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>.
Moreover, using (iv) and (v) of Lemma <a href="#Thmconj230" title="Lemma 30. ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ F.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix F Directional Convergence of the Nadaraya–Watson Estimator ‣ Generalization Bounds for Transformer-Based Next-Token Prediction in a Language Model" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>
we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx156" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\|P^{\perp}_{\bm{\alpha}}\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\mathbf{Z}_{2,T+1})\|^{2}_{2}|\mathbf{h}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\|P^{\perp}_{\bm{\alpha}}\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\mathbf{Z}_{2,T+1})\|^{2}_{2}|\mathbf{h}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E99.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{O}\Big(\lambda^{2\beta}+\frac{1}{T\varphi_{W}(\lambda)^{r_{2}}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{O}\Big(\lambda^{2\beta}+\frac{1}{T\varphi_{W}(\lambda)^{r_{2}}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">and for some <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx157" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\big[\|P_{\bm{\alpha}}\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\mathbf{Z}_{2,T+1})\|_{2}&lt;c|\mathbf{h}\big]\lesssim\frac{1}{T\varphi_{W}(\lambda)^{r_{2}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>𝜶</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐡</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\big[\|P_{\bm{\alpha}}\widehat{\mathbf{m}}_{\lambda}(\mathbf{Z}_{2,T+1})\|_{2}&lt;c|\mathbf{h}\big]\lesssim\frac{1}{T\varphi_{W}(\lambda)^{r_{2}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Here, the implicit constants and <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> depend only on <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{1},m_{2},\delta_{1},\delta_{2},r_{1},r_{2},\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathcal{C}^{\beta_{2}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{1},m_{2},\delta_{1},\delta_{2},r_{1},r_{2},\|\mathbf{h}\|_{\mathcal{C}^{\beta_{2}}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since the Euclidean distance between two unit vectors is upper bounded by their angle, it holds</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex372" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
